## 4. Hands-on CKA Exam Practice Drills

### Drill 1: Inspect and Add Helm Repositories

1. Check currently configured Helm repositories:
   `helm repo list`
1. Search for available charts in `prometheus-community`:
   `helm search repo prometheus-community`

### Drill 2: Override Helm Chart Values via CLI

1. Run `helm show values prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack | head -n 30` to inspect configurable properties.
1. Upgrade the release to adjust scrape intervals:
   `helm upgrade kube-prometheus prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack -n monitoring --reuse-values --set prometheus.prometheusSpec.scrapeInterval=15s`

### Drill 3: Create a Custom ServiceMonitor

1. Create a ServiceMonitor to scrape a target application in the `default` namespace.
1. Verify Prometheus discovers the new target via the Prometheus web UI (`Status -> Targets`).

### Drill 4: Inspect GatewayClass, Service Patching, and Gateway Creation

1. Verify the `nginx` GatewayClass is accepted by the controller:
   `kubectl get gatewayclass nginx -o yaml`
1. Practice imperative service patching (useful if controller service defaults to `LoadBalancer` with pending external IP):
   `kubectl patch service/ngf-nginx-gateway-fabric -n nginx-gateway -p '{"spec": {"type": "NodePort"}}'`
   Inspect the assigned NodePorts:
   `kubectl get svc -n nginx-gateway`
1. Deploy the Gateway resource (`cka-lab-gateway` on port 80 HTTP) from `~/cka/networking/03-gateway-api/`:
   `kubectl apply -f ~/cka/networking/03-gateway-api/cka-lab-gateway.yaml`
1. Verify the Gateway resource is accepted and programmed:
   `kubectl get gateway cka-lab-gateway`

### Drill 5: Connect Gateway API HTTPRoute to httpbin-go & Test Host Isolation

1. Deploy the lightweight httpbin-go backend (if not already running):
   `./install-httpbin-go.sh`
1. Apply the HTTPRoute matching hostname `httpbin.example.local` forwarding to `httpbingo:80`:
   `kubectl apply -f ~/cka/networking/03-gateway-api/cka-lab-httproute.yaml`
1. Verify the HTTPRoute is bound to the gateway:
   `kubectl get httproute cka-lab-httproute`
1. Test positive hostname routing (returns HTTP 200 from `httpbingo`):
   `curl -i -H "Host: httpbin.example.local" http://192.168.56.20:30080/`
1. Test negative hostname filtering (returns HTTP 404 Not Found from NGINX Gateway Fabric data plane):
   `curl -i -H "Host: unmatched.example.local" http://192.168.56.20:30080/`
